so the last chance qualifier for the  recent valerian astro clash was this  past weekend and dignitas and fallacy  both earned spots in the main event but  after one of fallacy's players mars  posted a clip from their final match on  twitter some members of the community  began questioning the legitimacy of  their wins to put it simply it looks  like her boyfriend may have been playing  all of the matches instead of her  [Music]  before i get into the video i just want  to let you guys know that we'll be  co-streaming evo on our twitch channel  from august 5th to 7th so if you're into  fighting games then make sure to check  it out this is even flying to canada so  it's going to be a lot of fun alright so  first off let's talk about what exactly  astral clash is it's a tournament hosted  by gen g and gallarants for the best  female identifying valorman players in  north america to compete for a ten  thousand dollar prize pool this past  weekend was the last chance qualifier  for the event and there were two final  spots up for grabs finish top two and  you'd earn yourself a trip to california  to compete in the main event paid for by  gen g when the qualifier got underway on  saturday fallacy looked like one of the  best teams and one of their players was  popping off mars finished their first  two matches with 351 and 295 acs  respectively which was higher than any  other player in the server she continued  to dominate in the semis and even the  finals where fallacy took down dignitas  who are a top 10 team within the game  changers scene according to vlr's  rankings it was an impressive run from  fallacy and after the match mars even  posted this crazy 1v4 ace clutch on  twitter  one enemy  [Music]  it was a pretty solid clutch if you ask  me but this is also where our story  starts to get pretty interesting you see  after mars posted that clip some members  of the community began questioning  whether or not it was actually her plan  later that night the twitter account  nice keybinds posted a google doc titled  account sharing concerns in gallaran's  astral clash the doc suggested that mars  had somebody else play on her account  throughout the entirety of the last  chance qualifier and that they believed  it was her boyfriend and xtsm academy  player pain within the dock are  screenshots comparing all of mars's  settings to payons some of the  screenshots were blurry though so i went  ahead and grabbed some clips from their  twitch channels that relate to the dock  on the left is a clip from mars stream  and on the right is a clip from paying  stream if we look closely then we can  see that mars uses the f key for her  first ability and payon uses the default  key which is c mars uses a cyan dot  crosshair while her boyfriend uses a  white crosshair and you can also see  that payon uses a slightly larger  minimap on top of that payon has also  posted clips on his twitter account that  show him using the discord overlay  something that isn't seen in any of  mars's past clips but is present in the  clip that she posted after the qualify  the dock also mentions that mars fps is  typically lower than what it is in the  clip it's quite a bit higher and in a  similar range to what pan averages now  even after all this i'm sure there are  some of you out there who are thinking  oh well she decided to try out her  boyfriend's settings and yeah that's a  possibility but i'm not sure if a simple  change to her settings could justify the  improved performance within the server  mars acs prior to astral clash was in  the low to mid hundreds but throughout  the last chance qualifier her acs was  291. if we look at payon's profile on  valorent tracker then we can also see  that he was playing ranked with the team  on july 19th without mars i reached out  to both of them for comment but  unfortunately didn't hear back from them  the final section of the google doc  mentions a past controversy with fallacy  they fielded two substitutes in the past  to change their twitter bio to display  non-binary before an event and after the  event one of them even removed it from  their profile so what does this mean  well if the allegations are true then  not only did fallacy break gallaran's  rules by fielding a male identifying  competitor but that would also mean that  mars broke riot's terms of service  section 1.5 of riot's tos states that  you can't share your account or login  credentials with anyone and you can't  sell transfer or allow any other person  to access your account or login  credentials or offer to do so by  breaking riot's tos you aren't just at  risk of losing the ability to compete  you're at risk of losing the ability to  play the game altogether if they  terminate your account but as long as  events or qualifiers continue to be  played online situations like this could  keep popping up genji did release a  statement today announcing that team  fallacy are suspended from competing in  the astral clash live finals and that  they will not be permitted in any  gallerance tournaments until riot  finishes their investigation riot  haven't released a statement at the time  of writing this but this just adds to a  long list of problems within the game  changer scene it seemed as though almost  every week there's some sort of drama  and riot notoriously haven't always  pleased the community with their rulings  game changers is meant to be a place  where women and marginalized genders can  compete and grow within the community so  i hope riot steps up and fixes things  because right now there are some people  making a mockery of it and it's not fair  to those who want to play and feel safe  while doing so  [Music]  you
 

